## Multi-Agent Workflow

### Before Starting Work
1. Check `.cursor/tasks/ACTIVE_TASKS.md` for conflicts
2. Review your agent role definition in `.cursor/agents/`
3. Create a task entry if modifying shared files
4. Review `docs/multi-agent/INTEGRATION_POINTS.md` for coordination needs

### Agent Role Definitions
- Agent roles defined in `.cursor/agents/` directory
- Each agent has primary scope, modification permissions, and forbidden files
- Review agent-specific documentation before starting work

### Communication Protocol
- Document significant changes in `.cursor/comms/change_log.md`
- Update task status in `.cursor/tasks/ACTIVE_TASKS.md`
- Coordinate with other agents before modifying shared files

## Error Handling

### GUI Errors
- Use `messagebox` for user-facing errors
- Log errors to console for debugging
- Provide fallback behavior when assets fail to load

### Game Logic Errors
- Validate inputs before processing
- Handle edge cases gracefully
- Use try-except blocks for file operations
- Provide meaningful error messages

## Performance Considerations

### Asset Loading
- Cache loaded images to prevent reloading
- Use lazy loading for non-critical assets
- Optimize image sizes before loading

### GUI Responsiveness
- Use `after()` for non-blocking operations
- Avoid blocking operations in main thread
- Update UI incrementally for long operations

## Documentation Standards

### Code Documentation
- All public functions must have docstrings
- Include parameter descriptions and return types
- Document exceptions that may be raised

### Project Documentation
- Update `README.md` when adding major features
- Update `MVP_ROADMAP.md` when completing tasks
- Document API changes in `docs/multi-agent/INTEGRATION_POINTS.md`

## Git Workflow

### Commit Messages
- Use clear, descriptive commit messages
- Reference task IDs when applicable
- Group related changes in single commits

### Branching Strategy
- Use feature branches for new development
- Merge to main after testing
- Coordinate merges when multiple agents work on same files

